<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in">Section 1.2 <U>Digital Currency
Payment.</U></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&#31532;</FONT>1.2<FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&#33410;
<B><U>&#25968;&#23383;&#36135;&#24065;&#25903;&#20184;</U></B>&#12290;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in">(a) The Purchaser shall satisfy
payment of the Purchase Price by delivering a number of units of Solv-BTC having a U.S. Dollar value equal to the Purchase Price. The
U.S. Dollar value of each unit of Solv-BTC shall be equal to the spot price of one (1) Solv-BTC as reported by CoinMarketCap (coinmarketcap.com)
at 5:00 p.m. New York City time on the business day immediately preceding the date of pricing (the &ldquo;Reference Time&rdquo;).</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in">The number of units of Solv-BTC
to be delivered at the Closing shall be calculated by dividing the Purchase Price by the Reference Rate (as defined above), rounded down
to four (4) decimal places.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in">The Company shall provide
the Purchaser with its designated digital wallet address for receiving the Solv-BTC at least three (3) Business Days prior to the Closing
Date. The Purchaser shall initiate the transfer of the requisite amount of Solv-BTC to the designated wallet address on or before the
Closing Date and shall provide the Company with reasonable evidence of such transfer, including the blockchain transaction hash and confirmation.
The Purchaser&rsquo;s obligation to pay the Purchase Price shall be deemed fully satisfied only upon confirmation on the applicable blockchain
that the Company has received the full amount of Solv-BTC in its designated digital wallet. If the spot price of Solv-BTC reported by
CoinMarketCap is unavailable or materially disrupted at the Reference Time, the Reference Rate shall instead be determined by reference
to a second independent and internationally recognized pricing source agreed by the Parties in writing. If, as of 5:00 p.m. New York City
time on the Business Day immediately preceding the Closing Date, the aggregate U.S. Dollar value of the Solv-BTC required to be delivered
hereunder (valued at the then-current spot price reported by CoinMarketCap) is less than ninety-five percent (95%) of the aggregate Purchase
Price, the Purchaser shall deliver at the Closing such additional Solv-BTC as is necessary so that the aggregate U.S. Dollar value so
delivered is not less than the aggregate Purchase Price.</P>

