<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in">Section 3.11 No Hedging or
Short Sales. From the date hereof until the expiration of the applicable Regulation S distribution compliance period (or, if Section 4(a)(2)/Regulation
D is relied upon, the date that is six (6) months after the Closing Date), neither the Purchaser nor any of its Affiliates nor any person
acting on its behalf shall, directly or indirectly, (i) engage in any &ldquo;short sale&rdquo; (as defined in Rule 200 of Regulation SHO
under the Exchange Act) of the Shares, or (ii) effect any hedge, put, collar, swap or other derivative transaction that transfers, in
whole or in part, the economic consequences of ownership of the Units, Shares or Warrants, whether settled in securities, cash or otherwise,
except in each case in compliance with the Securities Act. The Purchaser acknowledges that the foregoing restriction is a material inducement
to the Company&rsquo;s issuance of the Units.</P>

